 Kubernetes Deployment & Service using YAML (Date: 03/04/2025)

🔹 Deployment Configuration (Pod & ReplicaSet)
```yaml
# File: blue-deployment.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: blue-deploy
  namespace: blue-ns
spec:
  replicas: 5
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: ipl
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: ipl
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: c-1
          image: daviddocker526/ipl-srh:latest
          ports:
            - containerPort: 80
```

 Steps:
- `kubectl create ns blue-ns`
- `vi blue-deployment.yaml` (Edit with `i`, save with `:wq`)
- `kubectl apply -f blue-deployment.yaml`
- `kubectl get deployment -n blue-ns`
- `kubectl get rs -n blue-ns`
- `kubectl get pods -n blue-ns`
- `kubectl describe pod <pod-name> -n blue-ns`

---

🔹 Service Configuration
```yaml
# File: blue-service.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: blue-service
  namespace: blue-ns
spec:
  selector:
    app: ipl
  ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 80
      targetPort: 80
  type: LoadBalancer
```

 Service Types:
1. `ClusterIP`: Default; internal cluster access.
2. `NodePort`: Exposes service on each node’s IP at a static port.
3. `LoadBalancer`: Provides an external IP (not supported on Killercoda).
4. `ExternalName`: Maps a service to a DNS name.

Commands:
- `kubectl apply -f blue-service.yaml`
- `kubectl get all -n blue-ns`
- (Killercoda won’t show external IP due to free tier)

---

## 🔹 Other Useful Commands:
- `kubectl delete pod <pod-name> -n blue-ns`
- To change replica count:
  - Edit YAML → `replicas: 1`
  - `kubectl apply -f blue-deployment.yaml`
- Cleanup:
  - `kubectl delete deployment blue-deploy -n blue-ns`
  - `kubectl delete svc blue-service -n blue-ns`

